<Layout
  title="Lisbon D8 Digital Nomad Visa Income Threshold for Bootstrappers"
  description="Comprehensive guide for software bootstrappers applying for Portugal's D8 Digital Nomad Visa: €3,280/mo remote income proof, dividend qualification, and AIMA processing times."
  canonical="https://site-9-inky.vercel.app/lisbon-d8-visa-minimum-income-bootstrappers/"
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-emerald-400">FounderRunway</a> / <span>Nomad Visas</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-6">
      Lisbon D8 Digital Nomad Visa Income Threshold for Bootstrappers
    </h1>

    <div class="bg-emerald-950/20 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500 border-y border-r border-emerald-500/30 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-xl mb-10">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 font-mono mb-2">
        ⚡ Quick Answer: Portugal D8 Bootstrapper Threshold
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed">
        To qualify for Portugal's D8 Digital Nomad Visa in 2026, bootstrapped founders must demonstrate <strong>monthly remote income of at least €3,280</strong> (4x the national minimum wage of €820). Founders can prove this via consistent monthly Stripe/Paddle payouts into a corporate account with formal consulting contracts or documented shareholder dividend distribution resolutions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Acceptable Proof of Income for Solo Founders</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-300 mb-8 list-disc pl-5">
      <li><strong>Foreign Corporate Dividends</strong>: 6 months of corporate bank statements coupled with board resolutions and CPA certification demonstrating sustained distributions exceeding €3,280/mo.</li>
      <li><strong>Consulting / B2B Retainers</strong>: Formal written agreements with offshore entities specifying monthly compensation in USD, EUR, or GBP.</li>
      <li><strong>Liquid Capital Buffer</strong>: While not explicitly codified as income, depositing €39,360 (12 months of minimum income) into a Portuguese bank account (Millennium BCP or Novo Banco) drastically increases approval probability at AIMA.</li>
    </ul>

